3. Energy Microgrid: Formal Model and Stability

Definition 3.1 (DC Microgrid State). The energy system state is:

E_t = [SOC_t, P_{solar,t}, P_{load,t}, V_{bus,t}, T_{bat,t}]

Dynamics:

SOC_{t+1} = SOC_t + \frac{\eta_c P_{solar,t} - P_{load,t}/\eta_d}{E_{cap}} \Delta t

subject to:

SOC_{min} \leq SOC_t \leq SOC_{max}

V_{bus,min} \leq V_{bus,t} \leq V_{bus,max}

Theorem 3.1 (Microgrid Stability). The DC bus voltage V_{bus}(t) is asymptotically stable under the control law:

u_t = -K(V_{bus,t} - V_{ref})

if the feedback gain K satisfies:

K > \frac{1}{2 C_{dc} R_{eq}}

where C_{dc} is the bus capacitance and R_{eq} is the equivalent load resistance.

Proof. Consider the Lyapunov candidate:

V(V_{bus}) = \frac{1}{2}(V_{bus} - V_{ref})^2

The time derivative along system trajectories:

\dot{V} = (V_{bus} - V_{ref}) \dot{V}_{bus}

From the bus dynamics:

C_{dc} \dot{V}_{bus} = I_{in} - I_{load} = I_{in} - \frac{V_{bus}}{R_{eq}}

With control I_{in} = K(V_{ref} - V_{bus}):

\dot{V} = (V_{bus} - V_{ref}) \left[ -\frac{K}{C_{dc}}(V_{bus} - V_{ref}) - \frac{V_{bus} - V_{ref}}{C_{dc} R_{eq}} \right]

= -\left(\frac{K}{C_{dc}} + \frac{1}{C_{dc} R_{eq}}\right)(V_{bus} - V_{ref})^2 < 0

for all V_{bus} \neq V_{ref} when K > -1/R_{eq}, which holds for positive gains. ∎

Corollary 3.1 (Battery Autonomy Prediction). The predicted autonomy time is:

T_{autonomy} = \frac{(SOC_t - SOC_{reserve}) \cdot E_{cap}}{\mathbb{E}[\hat{P}_{load}] - \mathbb{E}[\hat{P}_{solar}]}

where the expectation is over the forecast horizon.

